# nlang: natural-language statements, with an LLM as the semantic oracle.
#
# See demos/README.md for how to run this script.
## Run without OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and TAU_NLANG_API_KEY to see
## the keyless answers; with a key, the oracle calls its provider's service.

# An nlang element is a phrase. The Boolean operations compose phrases and
# need no oracle. nothing and everything are bottom and top:

{ mammals }:nlang
{ mammals }:nlang | { large birds }:nlang
{ mammals }:nlang'
n { nothing }:nlang
n { everything }:nlang
n { mammals }:nlang | { nothing }:nlang

# Deciding whether two phrases denote the same set takes the oracle. Without a
# key every such question gets the conservative answer: not empty, not
# universal, not equivalent. A warning, printed once, says so (it appears at
# the first nlang element above). The equality of two distinct phrases
# therefore fails here, whatever a model would say:

sat { mammals }:nlang = { birds }:nlang

# The same phrase is equal to itself, and a phrase meets its own complement in
# bottom, on the structure of the phrases alone:

sat { mammals }:nlang = { mammals }:nlang
sat { mammals }:nlang & { mammals }:nlang' = { nothing }:nlang

# solve answers with a phrase:

solve x:nlang = { mammals }:nlang

# Streams carry phrases like any other type:

realizable G (F (o7[t]:nlang = {the sun is shining}:nlang))

# The oracle is set by options of the same names on the command line, in the
# environment and in the REPL. The key is never read back; get says only
# whether it is set:

get nlang-provider
get nlang-api-key
set nlang-provider anthropic
get nlang-provider
set nlang-model claude-opus-5-5
get nlang-model

# An empty text goes back to the default. The endpoint and the timeout belong
# to the same family; nlang-http-timeout is in seconds:

set nlang-provider ""
set nlang-model ""
get nlang-endpoint
get nlang-http-timeout

# A verdict about phrases that are not structurally equal is reliable only with
# a key: put it in TAU_NLANG_API_KEY, or in the key of the provider, before
# starting tau.

quit
